## Interface: 16001
## Title: Sane UI
## Notes: A sane user interface, built in modules. This is the part every module needs, with Sane UI's options (Esc > Options > AddOns > Sane UI, or /sane options) and the game settings it keeps the same on all your characters. The modules are listed below it: switch each one on or off by itself. Type /sane.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## SavedVariables: SaneUIDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: SaneUICharDB
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Gear_01
## AddonCompartmentFunc: SaneUI_OnAddonCompartmentClick
## X-License: MIT

# Core is the addon every module depends on. Saved.lua describes the settings of all of them,
# Profiles.lua keeps them: in a profile (Accountwide, at first, for every character) or a character's own.
Core.lua
# Small helpers for every module: the game's words, colours, pixels, tooltips, pools, dialogs, fonts,
# sounds, and frames of the game's lent for a while
Kit.lua
# Plain values as a line of text and back (a profile to share)
Serial.lua
# The kinds of motion a window's size can have (Glide, Swing, Even, Instant): before Saved.lua,
# which describes the general switch that chooses one
Motion.lua
Saved.lua
Profiles.lua
# What every window can use: places at the screen's edges to dock to, Esc, a watch on the mouse, a plate with
# round corners, background and border, moving (by a title bar, or in Blizzard's Edit Mode, chosen there with its
# dialog) and sizing (in Edit Mode), opening under the mouse, filling the screen from its screen edge, a title bar
# with a fuzzy search, views behind tabs, the game's own window kept out of sight while ours is chosen (the
# holder), and a progress bar
Dock.lua
EditMode.lua
Escape.lua
Watch.lua
Fuzzy.lua
Shape.lua
Skin.lua
Edge.lua
Window.lua
Views.lua
Selection.lua
Holder.lua
Expand.lua
Bar.lua
# The words of Sane UI's keys in the game's key bindings (what they do: Bindings.xml, read by the game itself)
Bindings.lua
# /sane window: a window to try them with
Demo.lua
# The data framework: Sane UI's own databases, loaded on demand from the data packs (SaneUI_Data_*), and the
# scheduler that does their long work in steps, a few milliseconds a frame (Doc/guides/data.md)
Data\Steps.lua
Data\Codec.lua
Data\Data.lua
# What each of the account's characters has (bags, bank, worn), kept in the pack Characters' saved variable
Data\Characters.lua
# Sync: the game's own settings kept with Sane UI's settings, a part per options page of the game
# and a few for what is on none (Edit Mode layout, chat windows, own channels). Pages.lua is made
# by dev/tools/sync-pages from Blizzard's options code.
Sync\Sync.lua
Sync\Data\Pages.lua
Sync\Layout.lua
Sync\Chat.lua
Sync\Game.lua
# Settings: the options, last: they show what everything above describes. The pages are put up
# at login, their controls made when the options are first opened.
Settings\Settings.lua
Settings\Panel.lua
Settings\Tabbed.lua
Settings\Profiles.lua
Settings\Synced.lua
# The page Sane UI: links (Discord, website, GitHub) and feedback
Settings\About.lua
Settings\Data\CVarLabels.lua
Settings\CVars.lua
Settings\Banner.xml
Settings\CVars.xml
